# NOTE: Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored (and `*.lock` is not blanket-ignored,
# which used to catch it). This workspace produces shipped
# *binaries* (razer-tray.exe / razer-cli.exe), and for binaries Cargo's own guidance
# is to commit the lockfile: it makes a release build reproducible and makes a
# dependency change visible in review rather than silently picked up on someone
# else's machine. (It is left out of version control only for libraries.)

# Workspace and cursor files (keep local only)
*.code-workspace
.cursor/
*.mdc

# Session documentation (not for repo)
*RECOVERED*.md
*MERGE*.md
*MERGED*.md
*SUMMARY*.txt
*PR_SUMMARY*.md
COMPARISON_WITH*.md
SYSTEM_CONFIGURATION*.md
RAZER_TRAY*.md
FINAL_STATUS.md
.local-notes/

# Helper scripts (local development)
*.env
start-razer-tray-quiet.sh
test-*.sh

# b-helper (separate project, not for upstream PR)
b-helper/
